WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.924
Validation starts with basic GPU detection.

00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:10.947
Confirm that the system sees the device, the driver is loaded, and the expected management tools report useful status.

00:00:10.947 --> 00:00:15.502
Check VRAM, utilization, temperature, power, and running processes.

00:00:15.502 --> 00:00:23.458
These checks tell you whether the system recognizes the hardware and whether anything is already consuming resources.

00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:26.313
The next step is an AI runtime smoke test.

00:00:26.313 --> 00:00:37.056
Run a simple inference task through the same path the real workload will use: host Python environment, container, notebook, inference server, or API endpoint.

00:00:37.056 --> 00:00:41.816
Confirm that acceleration is active, not just that the model responds.

00:00:41.816 --> 00:00:48.071
CPU fallback can make a test appear successful while hiding the fact that the GPU is unused.

00:00:48.071 --> 00:00:56.502
Performance checks should look at prompt processing speed, generation speed, memory use, temperature, power, and throttling.

00:00:56.502 --> 00:01:03.438
For vision or embedding workflows, use task-appropriate metrics such as processing time or throughput.

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:08.129
Compare results against expected behavior for the model and hardware.

00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:16.628
A sudden performance drop may indicate driver issues, thermal limits, wrong runtime settings, or an unintended fallback path.

00:01:16.628 --> 00:01:21.728
Distinguish driver problems from model, runtime, or configuration problems.

00:01:21.728 --> 00:01:26.080
Out-of-memory errors may come from model size or context length.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.907
Slow generation may come from CPU execution rather than driver failure.

00:01:30.907 --> 00:01:35.803
Container visibility issues may be permissions or runtime configuration.

00:01:35.803 --> 00:01:43.010
A structured validation checklist helps narrow the fault domain before reinstalling drivers unnecessarily.
